  "result": "I added the `refunded` state and tests for it, and all 11 tests pass (`python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t .`).\n\n**What changed**\n- **`shop/orders.py`**: `refunded` is now in `STATES`. In `ALLOWED`, `paid` and `shipped` can both move to `refunded`, and `refunded` has no transitions out.\n- **`shop/reports.py`**: no change needed. `sales_by_customer` only counts orders in `(\"paid\", \"shipped\")`, so refunded orders are already left out. No other code or doc in the repo lists the states.\n- **`tests/test_orders.py`**: new tests check that:\n  - `paid` and `shipped` orders can move to `refunded`;\n  - a refunded order can't move to any state;\n  - `new` and `cancelled` orders can't move to `refunded`;\n  - `sales_by_customer` leaves out refunded orders but still counts paid and shipped ones.\n\nI decided that `new` and `cancelled` orders can't be refunded, since neither was ever paid.\n\nNothing is committed. The test run left untracked `__pycache__` directories.\n\nToken Beggar: about 1.56x less spend than claude-opus-5-5 high alone (measured, multi_file)",
